{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1452566-v20-can-you-only-ever-have-3-paths-in-necromancy","id":1452566,"title":"[V20] Can you only ever have 3 paths in Necromancy?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-16T18:27:08-07:00","id":1452566,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> [V20] Can you only ever have 3 paths in Necromancy?","content":"So the reason I ask this question is because of one second found on <b>page 160</b> of the book. It reads:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Cainite necromancer must learn at least three levels in his primary path before learning his first level in a secondary Necromancy path. He must then master the primary path (all five levels) before acquiring any knowledge of a third path. </div> </div> </div>I know that secondary paths have a different cost and all that, but this section is worded in a way that confuses me a bit. I am also aware that there is no limit for Thaumaturgy other then they have to be less then your primary path until you master said path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T19:37:46-07:00","id":1452570,"title":"","content":"All blood sorceries operate the same way. A sorcerer is limited in the number of paths they may have until they've gotten level 5 in their primary path; once they do that, it's game on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T20:12:28-07:00","id":1452573,"title":"","content":"I wonder if this mechanic was intended to keep min-maxers from cherry-picking the &quot;best&quot; powers out of every path to get the most bang for their experience points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T20:23:01-07:00","id":1452574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1452566-v20-can-you-only-ever-have-3-paths-in-necromancy?p=1452570#post1452570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All blood sorceries operate the same way. A sorcerer is limited in the number of paths they may have until they've gotten level 5 in their primary path; once they do that, it's game on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem with that is Thaumaturgy in V20 is only limited in the fact players can not have a secondary path of a higher level then their primary path until they reach level 5. As stated with the following quote:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Core Book pages 212 to 213</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As mentioned before, the first path a character learns is considered her primary path and increases automatically as the character advances in the Discipline itself. Secondary paths may be learned once the character has acquired two or more dots in her primary path, and they must be raised separately with experience points. Furthermore, a character\u2019s rating in her primary path must always be at least one dot higher than any of her secondary paths until she has mastered her primary path. Once the character has achieved the fifth level of her primary path, secondary paths may be increased to that level.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T20:24:19-07:00","id":1452575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1452566-v20-can-you-only-ever-have-3-paths-in-necromancy?p=1452573#post1452573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if this mechanic was intended to keep min-maxers from cherry-picking the &quot;best&quot; powers out of every path to get the most bang for their experience points.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> See I would believe that if they did the same to Thaumaturgy, but nope just Necromancy. No such rule anywhere in Thaumaturgy whatsoever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T23:26:49-07:00","id":1452584,"title":"","content":"It's because Necromancy is still the less developed version of Sorcery. Each edition brings it one step closer to Thaumaturgy, but it's always a little worse. In 1e and 2e it was a regular Discipline, then Revised and V20 made it into Blood Magic, but obviously less refined with strange systems and more limited applications with fewer Rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T23:38:34-07:00","id":1452586,"title":"","content":"&quot;<i>A Cainite necromancer must learn at least three levels in his primary path before learning his first level in a secondary Necromancy path.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> This first line sets a condition on when a Necromancer can acquire a second path.<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>He must then master the primary path (all five levels) before acquiring any knowledge of a third path.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> Similarly, this line is simply a condition on when a Necromancer *can* acquire a third path; nothing it says precludes a Necromancer from acquire a fourth path after. Elaborating on when a third path is possible makes sense when you've previously explained the conditions for acquiring a second. Unless other text expressly forbids acquiring a fourth path, it doesn't seem to be against RAW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T00:47:08-07:00","id":1452588,"title":"","content":"Ignoring V5, the World of Darkness has always enabled you to learn absolutely everything within your particular splat. You're not learning new powers, you're unlocking potential. A vampire can learn every discipline, a Mage can learn every sphere and move beyond their paradigm, and a Garou can theoretically learn every Gift (which isn't very realistic given their lifespans and the amount of Gifts available, but the point stands) Thus Necromancers can of course learn All the Paths. <br /> <br /> Also I think the -you need three levels- thing is really something masters enforce on their students, not something that really aught to be an ironclad rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T06:11:26-07:00","id":1452614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1452566-v20-can-you-only-ever-have-3-paths-in-necromancy?p=1452574#post1452574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Problem with that is Thaumaturgy in V20 is only limited in the fact players can not have a secondary path of a higher level then their primary path until they reach level 5. As stated with the following quote:</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a limitation on what level a blood sorcerer's <i>second</i> path may be, not a limitation on the number of paths they may have in total. The latter was the heart of the question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T06:26:05-07:00","id":1452615,"title":"","content":"Is there no NPC with 4 paths listed? Either way you can learn them all in time in my understanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T12:43:33-07:00","id":1452673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1452566-v20-can-you-only-ever-have-3-paths-in-necromancy?p=1452586#post1452586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;<i>A Cainite necromancer must learn at least three levels in his primary path before learning his first level in a secondary Necromancy path.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> This first line sets a condition on when a Necromancer can acquire a second path.<br /> <br /> \u201c<i>He must then master the primary path (all five levels) before acquiring any knowledge of a third path.</i>\u201d<br /> <br /> Similarly, this line is simply a condition on when a Necromancer *can* acquire a third path; nothing it says precludes a Necromancer from acquire a fourth path after. Elaborating on when a third path is possible makes sense when you\u2019ve previously explained the conditions for acquiring a second. Unless other text expressly forbids acquiring a fourth path, it doesn\u2019t seem to be against RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div> Fair enough. That said, the phrasing of the sentence to an average person, and even now to me, makes it seem as if 3 paths is the maximum. At least to my simple brain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1452566-v20-can-you-only-ever-have-3-paths-in-necromancy?p=1452588#post1452588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ignoring V5, the World of Darkness has always enabled you to learn absolutely everything within your particular splat. You\u2019re not learning new powers, you\u2019re unlocking potential. A vampire can learn every discipline, a Mage can learn every sphere and move beyond their paradigm, and a Garou can theoretically learn every Gift (which isn\u2019t very realistic given their lifespans and the amount of Gifts available, but the point stands) Thus Necromancers can of course learn All the Paths.<br /> <br /> <b>Also I think the -you need three levels- thing is really something masters enforce on their students, not something that really aught to be an ironclad rule.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nope part of the system section, meaning that\u2019s how the system restricts it for necromancers, not how the mentors do it. Note I say necromancers, as practitioners of Thaumaturgy are not bound by this same restriction, at all!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1452566-v20-can-you-only-ever-have-3-paths-in-necromancy?p=1452615#post1452615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there no NPC with 4 paths listed? Either way you can learn them all in time in my understanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, if I did this first I wouldn\u2019t have asked the question. I finally found a Giovanni NPC, and it took 2 days! Anyway, this helped me solidify the answer to me, thank you!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T13:14:55-07:00","id":1452683,"title":"","content":"My hunch is that the Three Path Limit for Necromancy is just a copy-paste carryover because prior to V20 there was only the Ash, Bone and Sepulchur paths for Necromancy in the Revised Core Book and the others were in different books or even listed as separate disciplines. V20 was intended to be a one-shot with EVERYTHING in it so all those others got thrown into Necromancy, but they missed the needed change to the associated text in the base description.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T13:23:55-07:00","id":1452684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1452566-v20-can-you-only-ever-have-3-paths-in-necromancy?p=1452673#post1452673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough. That said, the phrasing of the sentence to an average person, and even now to me, makes it seem as if 3 paths is the maximum. At least to my simple brain.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Nope part of the system section, meaning that\u2019s how the system restricts it for necromancers, not how the mentors do it. Note I say necromancers, as practitioners of Thaumaturgy are not bound by this same restriction, at all!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> See, if I did this first I wouldn\u2019t have asked the question. I finally found a Giovanni NPC, and it took 2 days! Anyway, this helped me solidify the answer to me, thank you!</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand the confusion, the statement is a bit ambiguous. Just breaking it down to make explaining easier <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's been a little bit since I've looked, but I think you're right that in V20 Thaumaturgy's rule is &quot;no other Path can exceed the primary Path,&quot; which is looser than Necromancy's &quot;you must have x in Primary path before your second and third Paths.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's fast and dirty, but the White Wolf Wiki is often a good place to start. Sometimes they have character sheets that include a source where you can confirm. Only took me a few minutes to find a Giovanni with more than three paths of Necromancy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T02:13:32-07:00","id":1452745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1452566-v20-can-you-only-ever-have-3-paths-in-necromancy?p=1452673#post1452673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Nope part of the system section, meaning that\u2019s how the system restricts it for necromancers, not how the mentors do it. Note I say necromancers, as practitioners of Thaumaturgy are not bound by this same restriction, at all!<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I know it's part of the system section, but have you considered what in universe reasons could keep it that way? <br /> <br /> I thought about giving it a purely magical reason but the alternative is far more interesting; that it's a deliberate policy designed to keep magic out of the hands of &quot;commoners&quot;, which has two practical uses; It lowers the amount of people interested in learning thaumaturgy (which can be quite threatening), and it increases the value of the few hardcore thaumaturges/necromancers. <br /> <br /> Necromancers/Thaumaturges benefit economically from having their practices hard to learn. If you're the only one who can banish spectres in the city, you're going to be able to demand good prices when someone needs a spectre banished. If many can banish spectres, your price plummets; even if people just know a bit more about how banishing spectres works your prices can suffer. The Tremere are good at exploiting this because they're a union and they're in the cities of other vampires who need their help. The Giovanni/Hecata are awful because they keep to their own cities mostly, but at least they hunt their competitors","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T09:47:14-07:00","id":1452793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1452566-v20-can-you-only-ever-have-3-paths-in-necromancy?p=1452745#post1452745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know it's part of the system section, but have you considered what in universe reasons could keep it that way?<br /> <br /> I thought about giving it a purely magical reason but the alternative is far more interesting; that it's a deliberate policy designed to keep magic out of the hands of &quot;commoners&quot;, which has two practical uses; It lowers the amount of people interested in learning thaumaturgy (which can be quite threatening), and it increases the value of the few hardcore thaumaturges/necromancers.<br /> <br /> Necromancers/Thaumaturges benefit economically from having their practices hard to learn. If you're the only one who can banish spectres in the city, you're going to be able to demand good prices when someone needs a spectre banished. If many can banish spectres, your price plummets; even if people just know a bit more about how banishing spectres works your prices can suffer. The Tremere are good at exploiting this because they're a union and they're in the cities of other vampires who need their help. The Giovanni/Hecata are awful because they keep to their own cities mostly, but at least they hunt their competitors</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how that translates into this almost at all. In fact, if that were true then wouldn't it be an optional rule the ST could revoke without invoking the Golden Rule? Mechanics like this usually have exceptions written in or near them, or in the more &quot;fun&quot; cases in the fucking back of the book, and usually say something along the lines of &quot;If your ST allows this&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T09:56:53-07:00","id":1452794,"title":"","content":"Bah, lazy rules getting in the way of good speculative developments. Mechanics like this often have alternative mechanics for them written in another book. In this case, there really are no alt rules to my knowledge, but in a lot of circumstances there are alt rules or new rules or... really poorly thought out rules that nobody should use (Looking at you, Diamonion) <br /> <br /> I would say the rule should be default, but perhaps a merit would be great allowing you to ignore the rule. STs are encouraged to BS merits after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}